  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nSum = Rs. 10000\n\nRate = 12%\n\nTime = 11over4 years\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nA = P(1 + R/100)T\n\nC.I = A - P\n\nHere,\n\nA = amount\n\nP = sum\n\nT = time\n\nR = rate\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nRate for last 1over4 years = 12% × 1over4 = 3%\n\nNow,\n\nA = 10000(1 + 12/100) × (1 + 3/100)\n\n⇒ 10000(112/100) × (103/100)\n\n⇒ 11536\n\nSo, C.I = 11536 - 10000\n\n⇒ Rs. 1536\n\nAgain,\n\n11over4 years = 15 months\n\nSo, T = 15/5 = 3\n\nRate = 12 × (5/12)\n\n⇒ 5%\n\nNow,\n\nA = 10000(1 + 5/100)³\n\n⇒ 10000(1 + 1/20)³\n\n⇒ 10000(21/20)³\n\n⇒ 10000 × (9261/8000)\n\n⇒ 11576.25\n\nSo, C.I = 11576.25 - 10000\n\n⇒ Rs. 1576.25\n\nDifference = 1576.25 - 1536\n\n⇒ 40.25 ≈ 40\n\n**∴ Required difference is Rs. 40.**",
